// NEGATIVE TEST — a range pattern has both endpoints (N6-03).
//
// The normative pattern production in `docs/specification/grammar.ebnf` gives
// exactly two range forms, `expression ".." expression` and
// `expression "..=" expression`, and both are closed. `1..` is named nowhere, so
// it is a form the language does not have rather than one nobody has written
// yet — and inventing "to the maximum integer" here would put a rule in the
// compiler that no reader of the spec could have predicted.
//
// The mirror spelling `..5` is refused by the same rule one function earlier, in
// the pattern parser's primary position. The two messages differ in which end is
// missing and agree on the clause the manifest pins.
fn main() {
    let v = match 4 {
        1.. => 1,
        _ => 0,
    };
    print_int(v);
}
